---
import { ArrowLeft, ExternalLink } from "@lucide/astro";

import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Case Study B | TrialDiff"
  description="A TrialDiff case study showing why late-stage timeline registry changes can matter."
>
  <main class="page-shell stack methodology-page">
    <a class="button" href="/">
      <ArrowLeft size={16} />
      Back to dashboard
    </a>

    <header class="panel panel-pad">
      <p class="eyebrow">Case Study B</p>
      <h1>Why late-stage timeline changes matter</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This case uses an in-corpus timeline record from NCT02942355. It shows how TrialDiff separates a factual
        registry movement from any claim about intent, quality, or wrongdoing.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="panel panel-pad disclaimer">
      <div class="disclaimer-inner">
        <div>
          Severity means review priority, not proven wrongdoing. This case study surfaces a major timeline movement for
          review; it does not determine whether the movement was scientifically justified.
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>Record</h2>
      <p>
        TrialDiff compares ClinicalTrials.gov versions 26 and 27 for NCT02942355, a Wake Forest University Health
        Sciences study titled "Trial of Anastrozole and Palbociclib in Metastatic HER2-Negative Breast Cancer."
      </p>
      <p>
        Evidence Record:
        <a href="/events/evt_NCT02942355_v26_v27_f30d5b213a35">
          evt_NCT02942355_v26_v27_f30d5b213a35
        </a>
      </p>
      <p>
        Canonical JSON:
        <a href="/events/evt_NCT02942355_v26_v27_f30d5b213a35.json">
          /events/evt_NCT02942355_v26_v27_f30d5b213a35.json
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>What Changed</h2>
      <p>
        The patch replaced both the primary completion date and completion date with <code>2028-06-30</code>. It also
        updated status verification and last-update registry fields.
      </p>
      <p>
        TrialDiff's value signal records a 731-day timeline movement. The changed paths are concentrated in the status
        module, which makes this record a cleaner teaching case than a large multi-module patch.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>Why It Was Ranked Critical</h2>
      <p>
        The timeline rule treated a movement greater than 365 days as a major slip, giving the event high base severity.
        The from-version timing context was <code>late_recruitment</code>, so the timing modifier escalated the final
        severity to critical.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>What This Supports</h2>
      <p>
        This record supports a narrow factual statement: between versions 26 and 27, trial timeline fields moved by 731
        days, the movement occurred in a late-recruitment context, and TrialDiff classified the amendment as a
        review-priority timeline event.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>What This Does Not Support</h2>
      <p>
        This case does not show misconduct, sponsor intent, scientific unjustifiability, manuscript non-disclosure, or
        regulatory non-compliance. It does not determine whether the amendment was a delay, a backfill, a correction, or
        an expected operational update.
      </p>
      <p>
        The correct next question is the record's own review question: what explains the major timeline movement, and
        does the amendment represent a delay, a backfill, or a correction?
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>External Source</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02942355">
          View NCT02942355 on ClinicalTrials.gov
          <ExternalLink size={14} />
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
